  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "When I've set ebucore:filename directly in my ruby code, a download of an object has this URI appended to its filename. e.g. `b10410557_006.tif ^^ http---www.w3.org-2001-XMLSchema#string`",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I don't see this in fedora 4.5.1; am no longer running 4.6 anywhere so I can't say whether it's there.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This appended string makes it so Mac and Windows OSes cannot choose a default application to open the file, so it's a bit of a usability issue.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Any sort of workaround would be appreciated; once I have these values in there is there something I can do to change each of them so they don't come out this way?",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Alternately, workarounds as they're going in via hydra/sufia would also be appreciated; here's the code I'm using:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://github.com/projecthydra/sufia/commit/bb3017d7ebc3ffe8ce9c5825c838faa64a050a9d"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://github.com/projecthydra/sufia/commit/bb3017d7ebc3ffe8ce9c5825c838faa64a050a9d",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
